{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340948",
      "title": "On-Demand Cache Invalidation with revalidatePath & revalidateTag",
      "lectureOrder": 188,
      "videoOrder": 174,
      "sourceHash": "caee9014484fedc0334dc2292090d5146def8c6de46f563681473bcc7867f711",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.93,
          "end": 3,
          "en": "So revalidatePath",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3,
          "end": 5.34,
          "en": "is another way of making sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.34,
          "end": 8.01,
          "en": "that cached data is thrown away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.01,
          "end": 10.35,
          "en": "And a key difference compared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.35,
          "end": 12.69,
          "en": "to setting dynamic, force dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.69,
          "end": 14.97,
          "en": "or using the noStore function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.97,
          "end": 18.36,
          "en": "or using the configuration on the fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.36,
          "end": 20.7,
          "en": "is that all those settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.7,
          "end": 23.7,
          "en": "either disable caching altogether",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.7,
          "end": 26.463,
          "en": "or set a certain caching time period.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 30.06,
          "en": "When calling revalidatePath,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.06,
          "end": 34.92,
          "en": "we instead revalidate some piece of the cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.92,
          "end": 38.85,
          "en": "on demand when we tell NextJS to do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.85,
          "end": 41.88,
          "en": "And that can be more efficient than disabling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.88,
          "end": 46.88,
          "en": "the cache forever or setting a timeframe for caching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.98,
          "end": 51,
          "en": "Because with that timeframe, we of course would get NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51,
          "end": 55.44,
          "en": "to re-fetch data every five seconds, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.44,
          "end": 57.15,
          "en": "which is redundant if the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.15,
          "end": 59.43,
          "en": "didn't change within those five seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.43,
          "end": 61.503,
          "en": "So that's a bit inefficient then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.4,
          "end": 65.64,
          "en": "That's the advantage of explicitly telling NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.64,
          "end": 69.09,
          "en": "to revalidate the cache, because if we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.09,
          "end": 72.12,
          "en": "as a Next developer know that some data changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.12,
          "end": 75.09,
          "en": "we can simply tell NextJS about that and, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.09,
          "end": 77.01,
          "en": "get the best of both worlds:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.01,
          "end": 79.11,
          "en": "as much caching as possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.11,
          "end": 81.63,
          "en": "but updated data when we need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.63,
          "end": 86.03999999999999,
          "en": "Now, revalidatePath can be configured in different ways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.03999999999999,
          "end": 87.9,
          "en": "and you can learn all about that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.9,
          "end": 90.15,
          "en": "in the official documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.15,
          "end": 93.47999999999999,
          "en": "The main idea simply is that you define the path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.47999999999999,
          "end": 95.85,
          "en": "So for example, '/messages'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.85,
          "end": 98.22,
          "en": "that users might visit on your website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.22,
          "end": 100.95,
          "en": "and all the data related to that path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.95,
          "end": 105.003,
          "en": "and the route cache related to that path will be deleted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.93,
          "end": 107.72999999999999,
          "en": "What's important to note, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.72999999999999,
          "end": 110.82,
          "en": "is that any nested paths and nested pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.82,
          "end": 114.66,
          "en": "will not have their data and route cache deleted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.66,
          "end": 118.38,
          "en": "and revalidated, unless you also specify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.38,
          "end": 120.78,
          "en": "a second argument here and set this to 'layout'.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.83,
          "end": 124.83,
          "en": "If you do that, you essentially tell NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.83,
          "end": 129.09,
          "en": "that it should revalidate this cache for this path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.09,
          "end": 133.203,
          "en": "and also revalidate the cache of all nested pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.1,
          "end": 136.95,
          "en": "If you instead set this setting to 'page'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.95,
          "end": 139.92000000000002,
          "en": "or omit it, since 'page' is the default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.92000000000002,
          "end": 142.47,
          "en": "only the cache of this specific page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.47,
          "end": 145.023,
          "en": "will be revalidated and cleared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.13,
          "end": 149.13,
          "en": "Hence, if you would want to clear all the cached data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.13,
          "end": 152.7,
          "en": "of all pages of your page, you would have to set the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.7,
          "end": 157.32,
          "en": "to just '/', so to the root path of the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.32,
          "end": 161.34,
          "en": "and add 'layout', and that would now clear the cache data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.34,
          "end": 165.333,
          "en": "and the route cache of all pages on your site.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.29,
          "end": 169.143,
          "en": "That's how revalidatePath works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.16,
          "end": 173.13,
          "en": "Of course, you can also call it multiple time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.13,
          "end": 176.43,
          "en": "if you would want to revalidate the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.43,
          "end": 178.56,
          "en": "of different pages like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.56,
          "end": 180.483,
          "en": "That would be possible as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.53,
          "end": 183.75,
          "en": "In addition to revalidatePath,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.75,
          "end": 187.83,
          "en": "there also is a revalidateTag function you can call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.83,
          "end": 190.557,
          "en": "that's also imported from 'next/cache'.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 191.82,
          "end": 196.82,
          "en": "And revalidateTag then takes a tag like 'msg' as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 199.98,
          "end": 202.82999999999998,
          "en": "But how does this function work now?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 202.82999999999998,
          "end": 206.64,
          "en": "Well, you can assign tags to requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.64,
          "end": 209.37,
          "en": "that fetch data that will be cached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.37,
          "end": 212.04,
          "en": "For example, here, when sending that fetch request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.04,
          "end": 216.21,
          "en": "I can add that configuration object with that next key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.21,
          "end": 219.66,
          "en": "And then there, besides setting that revalidate option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 219.66,
          "end": 223.05,
          "en": "you saw before, I can set up some tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.05,
          "end": 224.9,
          "en": "and that will be an array of strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.11,
          "end": 228.3,
          "en": "And here you can set up any tags you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.3,
          "end": 229.917,
          "en": "for example, 'msg'.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231,
          "end": 232.68,
          "en": "And you can assign multiple tags",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.68,
          "end": 234.903,
          "en": "to one request if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.1,
          "end": 238.86,
          "en": "Now, these tags will, under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.86,
          "end": 241.74,
          "en": "be connected to the cached data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 241.74,
          "end": 245.61,
          "en": "and if you then call revalidateTag with a certain tag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 245.61,
          "end": 248.58,
          "en": "NextJS will revalidate and throw away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.58,
          "end": 251.373,
          "en": "any cached data that has that tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.24,
          "end": 254.31,
          "en": "So that would allow you to clear the cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.31,
          "end": 257.31,
          "en": "of multiple pages if those different pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.31,
          "end": 260.94,
          "en": "would assign the same tags to their requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.94,
          "end": 264.99,
          "en": "So instead of calling revalidatePath multiple times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.99,
          "end": 267.93,
          "en": "for different pages, you could just use one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 267.93,
          "end": 269.82,
          "en": "and the same tag on different pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.82,
          "end": 272.28,
          "en": "and then just revalidate that tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.28,
          "end": 275.253,
          "en": "to clear all the cached data of those pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 276.99,
          "end": 278.46,
          "en": "Now to show you how this works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.46,
          "end": 282.65999999999997,
          "en": "I'll call revalidate tag with 'msg' as a tag here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.65999999999997,
          "end": 284.82,
          "en": "in this new message page component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 284.82,
          "end": 286.62,
          "en": "when that form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 286.62,
          "end": 288.24,
          "en": "And I'm not doing anything else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.24,
          "end": 289.77,
          "en": "with that submitted data right now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 289.77,
          "end": 291.93,
          "en": "but we'll change that soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 291.93,
          "end": 293.49,
          "en": "I'll comment out this line here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 293.49,
          "end": 296.67,
          "en": "so that I'm not storing anything in the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 299.4,
          "en": "so that I really just use that as a dummy function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 299.4,
          "end": 301.83,
          "en": "right now to show you revalidateTag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 302.743,
          "end": 307.47,
          "en": "And I did set the same tag here on my messages page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 307.47,
          "end": 311.55,
          "en": "And with that set up, if I restart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 311.55,
          "end": 315.513,
          "en": "my development server here and I restart the backend server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 316.56,
          "end": 319.17,
          "en": "you will see that if I reload this messages page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319.17,
          "end": 321.6,
          "en": "multiple times, I got no logs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.6,
          "end": 323.01,
          "en": "which hopefully makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 323.01,
          "end": 326.103,
          "en": "because we're caching and reusing data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 327.3,
          "end": 332.22,
          "en": "But because I assigned that tag and I revalidate that tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 332.22,
          "end": 335.13,
          "en": "after submitting the forum on the new message page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 335.13,
          "end": 336.87,
          "en": "if I go to the new message page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 336.87,
          "end": 338.94,
          "en": "and enter some message here, doesn't matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 338.94,
          "end": 342.3,
          "en": "we're not using it anyways, and I click send,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 342.3,
          "end": 346.23,
          "en": "you will see that now I got some logs here;",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 346.23,
          "end": 350.82,
          "en": "because I revalidated the cached data connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 350.82,
          "end": 353.7,
          "en": "to my request, to my fetch request here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 353.7,
          "end": 355.593,
          "en": "and hence it was resent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 356.64,
          "end": 360.663,
          "en": "And that's the idea behind revalidateTag and revalidatePath.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
